ting, establishes standards for companies to report in their financial statements information about operating segments, products, services, geographic areas, and major customers.","context":"(ai) Segment reporting","section":"ITEM 19.","block":3145,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-157849","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-16","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001810997","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1810997/000119312526157849/d36361d20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/d9f401197cd9ecd074228e2a2155f59a7654ee7b13fa0e4eb03d07f5d1c9b224.bin","sha256":"d9f401197cd9ecd074228e2a2155f59a7654ee7b13fa0e4eb03d07f5d1c9b224"}},{"id":"93cd7c0f8332d4fda8b30fbf1e59d980f3bc3589f222b35bbb8dcad3dd5f6f62","quote":"Based on the criteria established by ASC 280, the Group’s chief operating decision maker (“CODM”) has been identified as the Chief Executive Officer, who reviews consolidated revenue, gross profit and net loss when making decisions about allocating resources and assessing performance of the Group. As a whole and hence, the Group has only one reportable segment. As one reportable segment, the Group derives revenue from vehicle sales and the related business.","context":"ASC 280, Segment Reporting, establishes standards for companies to report in their financial statements information about operating segments, products, services, geographic areas, and major customers.","section":"ITEM 19.","block":3146,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001193125-26-157849","form":"20-F","filedAt":"2026-04-16","reportDate":"2025-12-31","cik":"0001810997","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1810997/000119312526157849/d36361d20f.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/d9f401197cd9ecd074228e2a2155f59a7654ee7b13fa0e4eb03d07f5d1c9b224.bin","sha256":"d9f401197cd9ecd074228e2a2155f59a7654ee7b13f